  "title": "Job 19",
  "display_title": "Job 19",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 19,
  "sortOrder": 18019,
  "verseCount": 29,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Then Job answered and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "How long will ye vex my soul, and break me in pieces with words?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "These ten times have ye reproached me: ye are not ashamed that ye make yourselves strange to me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "And be it indeed that I have erred, mine error remaineth with myself.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "If indeed ye will magnify yourselves against me, and plead against me my reproach:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Know now that God hath overthrown me, and hath compassed me with his net.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Behold, I cry out of wrong, but I am not heard: I cry aloud, but there is no judgment.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "He hath fenced up my way that I cannot pass, and he hath set darkness in my paths.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "He hath stripped me of my glory, and taken the crown from my head.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "He hath destroyed me on every side, and I am gone: and mine hope hath he removed like a tree.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "He hath also kindled his wrath against me, and he counteth me unto him as one of his enemies.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "His troops come together, and raise up their way against me, and encamp round about my tabernacle.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "He hath put my brethren far from me, and mine acquaintance are verily estranged from me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "My kinsfolk have failed, and my familiar friends have forgotten me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "They that dwell in mine house, and my maids, count me for a stranger: I am an alien in their sight.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "I called my servant, and he gave me no answer; I intreated him with my mouth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "My breath is strange to my wife, though I intreated for the children’s sake of mine own body.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Yea, young children despised me; I arose, and they spake against me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "All my inward friends abhorred me: and they whom I loved are turned against me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "My bone cleaveth to my skin and to my flesh, and I am escaped with the skin of my teeth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Have pity upon me, have pity upon me, O ye my friends; for the hand of God hath touched me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Why do ye persecute me as God, and are not satisfied with my flesh?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Oh that my words were now written! oh that they were printed in a book!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "That they were graven with an iron pen and lead in the rock for ever!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "For I know that my redeemer liveth, and that he shall stand at the latter day upon the earth:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "And though after my skin worms destroy this body, yet in my flesh shall I see God:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Whom I shall see for myself, and mine eyes shall behold, and not another; though my reins be consumed within me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "But ye should say, Why persecute we him, seeing the root of the matter is found in me?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:19:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "Be ye afraid of the sword: for wrath bringeth the punishments of the sword, that ye may know there is a judgment.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 19:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:19:29"
      }
    }
  ],
